Gate repaired: remote-tracking-ref work is green — `make build` passes again, and a worktree with a missing or symlinked `node_modules` now stops in one line instead of dying minutes into a Turbopack build.

- Cause of the exit-2 gate: this `git worktree` checkout had `node_modules` as a symlink to the main checkout's copy. Turbopack roots the project at the worktree and rejects a link that escapes it (`Symlink [project]/node_modules is invalid, it points out of the filesystem root`), while `test`/`lint`/`typecheck` follow the link happily — so only `build` broke. The worktree now carries its own real `node_modules/` (verified complete: 4251 entries / 1.3G, matching the main checkout) and `make build` exits 0.
- `Makefile`: the symlink/absence check is now a real `check-deps` prerequisite target listed first in `build` (ahead of `build-worker`) and in `check`, replacing the previous `CHECK_DEPS` recipe-line hack — recipe lines run only after every prerequisite, so esbuild and the whole vitest pass still ran before the failure surfaced. `check-deps` is `.PHONY` and deliberately has no `## ` help line, so `make help` is unchanged.
- Probe evidence: with a symlinked `node_modules`, `make build` now exits 2 with `node_modules is a symlink out of this checkout and Turbopack rejects it — run 'make install'` and esbuild never runs; with `node_modules` absent it names the missing install; `make -n check` shows `check-deps` first, then test/lint/typecheck/build/check-split.
- `CONTRIBUTING.md`: the "Before you open a PR" note now explains that a worktree needs its own real `node_modules` (spec 20), why the failure was previously late and build-only, and that `make build` / `make check` stop up front naming `make install`.
- Card feature work (unchanged this iteration, already committed): `src/server/integrity.ts` classifies `refs/remotes/**` outside `ralph/` as warnings surfaced as a `repo.integrity_warning` event (`src/server/stage.ts`, shown on the card Activity timeline in `src/app/card/[id]/page.tsx`), documented in `specs/19-shared-git-ref-noise.md`'s dated amendment plus `docs/SANDBOXING.md`, `docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md`, `docs/DESIGN_HISTORY.md`.
- Caveat for the operator: the dependency copy lives in the gitignored `node_modules/`, so it is not part of the commit. If a future worktree is provisioned with a symlinked `node_modules` again, the gate will now fail immediately with the `run 'make install'` message rather than mid-build — provisioning each worktree with real dependencies (`make install`) is the environment-side half of the fix.